# pkg.ttl — the Project-Knowledge-Graph (PKG) vocabulary (machine-readable form)
#
# [OPUS-4.8] sq-2m6zm.1 (epic sq-2m6zm). 🤖 SPARQ agent — dogfooding sparq as a
# project knowledge graph. Written while Fable unavailable; flag for re-review when
# Fable returns.
#
# This is the canonical, machine-readable rendering of the reuse-first ontology of
# `research/dogfooding-sparq-knowledge-graph.md` §2.3 (design record on PR #1063).
# It is byte-pinned against the Rust constants in `crates/sparq-kb/src/vocab.rs` by
# the `ttl_pins_match_rust_constants` sync test in that module — the two MUST NOT
# drift.
#
# DESIGN PRINCIPLE (copied from the maintainer's own `sec-prop` discipline,
# research/security-properties-ontology-design.md): the PKG mints almost NO net-new
# terms. PROV-O carries who/what/when/derived-from; SKOS carries concepts/topics;
# DCAT + FaBiO/FRBR + DC carry the source catalog; DQV models the quality axis
# (confidence/assurance as named, distinct quality measurements/metrics/dimensions);
# CiTO carries the typed citation + technique-relation edges; schema.org fills gaps;
# and the vendored `zkp-sparql` ontologies already define the Claim + Evidence +
# Confidence + Source pattern as `sig-impl:Assertion`. `pkg:Finding` GENERALISES that
# pattern; it does not fork it. Only FOUR bespoke predicates/classes are genuinely
# net-new (`pkg:exploredStatus`, `pkg:followUpPriority`, `pkg:confidence`,
# `pkg:couldBeMergedWith`) plus the single `pkg:dependsOn` owl:inverseOf
# `pkg:blockedBy` pair, plus the bd-task / source / technique scaffolding the design
# names. The DQV adoption (sq-2489d.3) adds NO net-new bespoke predicate: it reuses the
# standard DQV classes/properties and a small set of NAMED DQV-instance individuals
# (the quality dimension + per-axis metrics), and the technique-relation graph leans on
# the established CiTO terms `cito:extends` / `cito:usesMethodIn` instead of minting
# bespoke supersede/method predicates — so the bespoke surface shrinks, it does not
# grow. See PROVENANCE.md for the full reuse table and the live-ontology alignment
# verification (incl. DQV's W3C-Note status).
#
# The `pkg:` namespace (https://sparq.dev/ns/pkg#) is a sparq-local namespace,
# consistent with `trust:` (https://sparq.dev/ns/trust#) and `zk:`
# (https://sparq.dev/ns/zk#). It is NOT minted/resolvable today; a future
# standardisation pass would rehome the net-new terms.
#
# FO CHOICE RATIFIED (sq-mztg8.5, 2026-07-06): schema.org-as-top is the PKG's top
# foundational ontology, ratified after Fable-subject Metric-1 re-run (PR #1603).
# No data changes required. Verdict record: research/provenance-driven-genai-kb.md §6
# item 5. Revisit trigger: if the fleet's KM-query tier moves predominantly to
# Fable-class models, re-run bench/fo-km Metric-1 before reopening.
#
# READ-PATH FACADE SELECTION (sq-mztg8.4, FO-bridge Phase 5): the facade STAYS
# schema.org-as-top — the "otherwise" branch of the phase, taken on the EVIDENCE, not
# by preference. gist is NOT promoted because the pre-registered kill-criterion K2
# ("if gist does not match-or-beat schema.org, gist-as-named-facade is dropped and
# schema.org-as-top stays the facade", research/fo-llm-bridge.md §4.3) has never been
# able to fire: the broadened Metric-1 round-2 arm set (sq-givgo) has NOT landed —
# bench/fo-km/overlays/ carries no gist (or BFO) overlay — so gist has never been
# measured against this PKG at any model tier. Metric 2 (sq-p5ro8) likewise remains
# EC2-deferred and sign-unstable, and reads on the rich-FO BACKBONE, not on the facade.
# The bridge axioms below are therefore unchanged; the schema.org facade they assert is
# now also surfaced to the agent's introspect stage by the `facade-terms` canned query
# (src/query/canned.rs), which the pkg:-filtered `schema-classes` card cannot show.
# Reopen trigger: sq-givgo lands a measured gist arm. Promoting gist is additionally a
# facade-IDENTITY values call (research/fo-llm-bridge.md §7 open question 3) and needs
# maintainer steer, so it is NOT taken here on evidence alone. [OPUS-5]

@prefix pkg:     <https://sparq.dev/ns/pkg#> .
@prefix prov:    <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#> .
@prefix skos:    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
@prefix dcat:    <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .
@prefix dqv:     <http://www.w3.org/ns/dqv#> .
@prefix fabio:   <http://purl.org/spar/fabio/> .
@prefix cito:    <http://purl.org/spar/cito/> .
@prefix frbr:    <http://purl.org/vocab/frbr/core#> .
@prefix bibo:    <http://purl.org/ontology/bibo/> .
@prefix schema:  <http://schema.org/> .
@prefix np:      <http://www.nanopub.org/nschema#> .
@prefix sigimpl: <https://w3id.org/zkp-sparql/sig-impl#> .
@prefix secx:    <https://w3id.org/zkp-sparql/sec-prop#> .
@prefix rdf:     <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs:    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix owl:     <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix xsd:     <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

# --- ontology metadata -------------------------------------------------------

pkg: a owl:Ontology ;
  rdfs:label "Project Knowledge Graph (PKG) vocabulary"@en-GB ;
  dcterms:description """A reuse-first vocabulary for storing a software project's own
knowledge — research findings with provenance + DQV-modelled quality (confidence +
assurance), sources with an explored-status, concepts, algorithms/techniques
(extends / uses-method-in / supersedes / alternative-to / mergeable-with /
implemented-by), and the bd task model — as RDF behind a SPARQL + SHACL + reasoning
surface. Generalises the vendored zkp-sparql sig-impl:Assertion reified-claim pattern
into pkg:Finding; reuses PROV-O, SKOS, DCAT, DQV, FaBiO/FRBR/DC, CiTO, schema.org, and
nanopublications. Companion: PROVENANCE.md (reuse table + live-ontology alignment
verification) and research/dogfooding-sparq-knowledge-graph.md (design record, PR
#1063); DQV is a W3C Working Group Note (see PROVENANCE.md)."""@en-GB ;
  rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/sparq-org/sparq/issues/1063> ;
  rdfs:comment "sparq-local namespace; the net-new terms would be rehomed by a standardisation pass."@en-GB .

# =============================================================================
# Source / Document — the source catalog (DCAT + FaBiO/FRBR + DC; mint only the
# explored-status + follow-up-priority axes)
# =============================================================================

pkg:Source a owl:Class ;
  rdfs:label "Source"@en-GB ;
  rdfs:comment "A bibliographic / documentary source of project knowledge (a paper, a research/ design record, a spec). Reuses fabio:Expression (the FRBR realisation of a work's content) and dcat:CatalogRecord (the catalog entry)."@en-GB ;
  rdfs:subClassOf fabio:Expression , dcat:CatalogRecord .

pkg:Document a owl:Class ;
  rdfs:label "Document"@en-GB ;
  rdfs:comment "A concrete document realising a Source (an in-repo file, a PDF, a web page). Reuses fabio:Expression; a pkg:Source frbr:realizationOf the work, a pkg:Document the in-repo/dereferenceable realisation."@en-GB ;
  rdfs:subClassOf fabio:Expression .

# --- the machine-extraction tier (sq-2489d.5). A pkg:MachineAgent is the prov:Agent a
#     machine-extracted Finding is prov:wasAttributedTo (e.g. agent:haiku-extractor). It
#     reuses prov:SoftwareAgent; it carries NO net-new predicate. It is the declarative
#     hook the literature-tier SHACL shapes (shapes/literature.shapes.ttl §4.5) target:
#     a Finding attributed to a pkg:MachineAgent sits on the low-trust tier (must be
#     secx:Conjectured, bounded confidence, no dangling cito:citesAsEvidence). A
#     hand-authored Finding is NOT attributed to a pkg:MachineAgent, so those constraints
#     do not bind it. The extraction event itself is a plain prov:Activity (prov:used the
#     Source's abstract, prov:wasAssociatedWith the agent) — no new class needed.
pkg:MachineAgent a owl:Class ;
  rdfs:label "Machine agent"@en-GB ;
  rdfs:comment "A non-human software agent that produces Findings by extraction (e.g. a cheap-model literature extractor). Reuses prov:SoftwareAgent. A Finding prov:wasAttributedTo a pkg:MachineAgent is on the low-trust machine-extraction tier — see shapes/literature.shapes.ttl (research/provenance-driven-genai-kb.md §4.5). The extraction quality boundary is load-bearing: a cheap model hallucinates, so the tier is capped at secx:Conjectured with a bounded confidence and a grounding-verified citation; a machine extraction must never outrank a hand-authored Finding."@en-GB ;
  rdfs:subClassOf prov:SoftwareAgent .

# --- NET-NEW: the explored-status axis (a SKOS scheme so it is queryable +
#     extensible). Aligned to schema.org ActionStatusType via skos:closeMatch.
pkg:ExplorationStatus a skos:ConceptScheme ;
  rdfs:label "Source exploration status scheme"@en-GB ;
  dcterms:description "How far a source has been explored, so follow-up can be targeted at the un-explored ones."@en-GB .

pkg:exploredStatus a owl:ObjectProperty ;
  rdfs:label "explored status"@en-GB ;
  rdfs:comment "NET-NEW. The exploration state of a source (pkg:Unexplored | pkg:Exploring | pkg:Explored | pkg:DeadEnd) — the targeted-follow-up lever. No FAIR-friendly term in DCAT/DC carries the explored-vs-unexplored role for project knowledge, so it is minted."@en-GB ;
  rdfs:domain pkg:Source ;
  rdfs:range skos:Concept .

pkg:followUpPriority a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
  rdfs:label "follow-up priority"@en-GB ;
  rdfs:comment "NET-NEW. Integer ordering for which un-explored sources to read next (lower = sooner)."@en-GB ;
  rdfs:domain pkg:Source ;
  rdfs:range xsd:integer .

pkg:Unexplored a skos:Concept ; skos:inScheme pkg:ExplorationStatus ;
  skos:prefLabel "Unexplored"@en-GB ;
  skos:closeMatch schema:PotentialActionStatus .
pkg:Exploring a skos:Concept ; skos:inScheme pkg:ExplorationStatus ;
  skos:prefLabel "Exploring"@en-GB ;
  skos:closeMatch schema:ActiveActionStatus .
pkg:Explored a skos:Concept ; skos:inScheme pkg:ExplorationStatus ;
  skos:prefLabel "Explored"@en-GB ;
  skos:closeMatch schema:CompletedActionStatus .
pkg:DeadEnd a skos:Concept ; skos:inScheme pkg:ExplorationStatus ;
  skos:prefLabel "Dead end"@en-GB ;
  skos:closeMatch schema:FailedActionStatus .

# =============================================================================
# Concept / Topic — pure SKOS (no mint)
# =============================================================================

pkg:Topics a skos:ConceptScheme ;
  dcterms:title "sparq project topics"@en-GB .
# Every Finding/Source/Technique/Task tags itself with dcterms:subject -> a skos:Concept.

# =============================================================================
# Finding / Claim — GENERALISE sig-impl:Assertion (Claim + Evidence + Confidence
# + Source); PROV-O + CiTO; mint only the numeric confidence axis
# =============================================================================

pkg:Finding a owl:Class ;
  rdfs:label "Finding"@en-GB ;
  rdfs:comment "A reified discovery / claim about the project's domain — a generalisation of the vendored sig-impl:Assertion reified-verdict pattern from (signature-impl, security-property) verdicts to (any subject, any claim). Carries a verdict + justification + evidence (supporting/refuting sources) + a numeric confidence + an assurance basis + PROV-O lineage. SHACL (FindingShape) makes the source + confidence + assurance + non-filler justification MANDATORY."@en-GB ;
  rdfs:subClassOf sigimpl:Assertion , skos:Concept .

pkg:about a owl:ObjectProperty ;
  rdfs:label "about"@en-GB ;
  rdfs:comment "The subject the Finding is about (a pkg:Technique, a pkg:Source, a topic, …). rdfs:subPropertyOf dcterms:subject."@en-GB ;
  rdfs:subPropertyOf dcterms:subject ;
  rdfs:domain pkg:Finding .

pkg:verdict a owl:ObjectProperty ;
  rdfs:label "verdict"@en-GB ;
  rdfs:comment "The Finding's verdict, reusing sig-impl:yes / sig-impl:no / sig-impl:partial (per the design's reuse decision; §2.5 flags that a research verdict space may later diverge, in which case a pkg:-specific enum subclasses this without forking the pattern). ENUM-MAPPING CONVENTION (sq-2489d.8 / 2026-07-05): pkg:yes + secx:Proven = high-confidence asserted truth; pkg:yes + secx:Claimed = claimed fact (lower assurance); pkg:no + pkg:assurance X reverses polarity (claim is false, with assurance X). pkg:partial = nuanced/mixed result. A pkg:-specific research subclass ({holds/refuted/uncertain/superseded}) is deferred until literature ingestion measures strain on this generic enum (sq-2489d.6, Phase 5)."@en-GB ;
  rdfs:subPropertyOf sigimpl:verdict ;
  rdfs:domain pkg:Finding ;
  rdfs:range sigimpl:Verdict .

# --- NET-NEW (bespoke): numeric confidence axis (0..1). A convenience shorthand for
#     the dqv:value of a named dqv:QualityMeasurement (see the DQV quality-model block
#     below). Aligned to schema:Rating.
pkg:confidence a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
  rdfs:label "confidence"@en-GB ;
  rdfs:comment "NET-NEW (bespoke). The numeric confidence (0.0..1.0) attached to a Finding (epistemic weight) or a Source (reliability). schema:Rating is rating-of-a-creative-work and DPV has no 0..1 confidence literal, so a bounded decimal is minted; aligned to schema:Rating via skos:closeMatch. KEPT as a convenience shorthand (every canned query reads it directly), but DEFINED (sq-2489d.3) as the dqv:value of a named dqv:QualityMeasurement (pkg:ConfidenceMeasurement / pkg:SourceReliabilityMeasurement) — rdfs:subPropertyOf dqv:value, so a reasoner sees a pkg:confidence as a DQV measurement value. Orthogonal to pkg:assurance (the epistemic-basis metric)."@en-GB ;
  rdfs:subPropertyOf dqv:value ;
  rdfs:range xsd:decimal ;
  skos:closeMatch schema:Rating .

pkg:assurance a owl:ObjectProperty , dqv:Metric ;
  rdfs:label "assurance"@en-GB ;
  rdfs:comment "The epistemic basis of a Finding, reusing the sec-prop extension assurance axis secx:Proven / secx:Claimed / secx:Conjectured (research/security-properties-ontology-design.md §4.2.2, epic sq-0dksu). NOTE: those secx: IRIs are defined in that DESIGN record and are not yet shipped as a committed .ttl; they are referenced here by their stable w3id namespace so they unify when sq-0dksu ships. ALSO typed (sq-2489d.3) as a dqv:Metric in the pkg:EpistemicBasisDimension — the DQV-modelled home for the assurance axis. See PROVENANCE.md."@en-GB ;
  dqv:inDimension pkg:EpistemicBasisDimension ;
  rdfs:domain pkg:Finding .

# =============================================================================
# Quality model — DQV (sq-2489d.3). The principled, NAMED home for the quality axes
# (confidence/assurance) that pkg:confidence/pkg:assurance shorthand. NO net-new
# bespoke predicate is minted: these are INSTANCES of the standard DQV classes
# (dqv:Dimension / dqv:Metric / dqv:QualityMeasurement), exactly as pkg:Open etc. are
# instances of skos:Concept. A Finding's pkg:confidence is the dqv:value of a
# dqv:QualityMeasurement that dqv:isMeasurementOf one of these metrics, dqv:computedOn
# the Finding/Source. DQV carries prov:wasGeneratedBy/wasAttributedTo natively, so a
# measurement composes with sparq-prov for free; and pkg:Source already
# rdfs:subClassOf dcat:CatalogRecord (DQV's anchor), so the coupling is already paid.
# HONEST: DQV is a W3C Working Group Note (2016), not a Recommendation, and it models a
# measurement — it does NOT give confidence PROPAGATION through joins (the Hartig /
# tSPARQL gap is real and orthogonal). See PROVENANCE.md.
# =============================================================================

# The two quality dimensions the PKG measures along (instances of dqv:Dimension).
pkg:EpistemicWeightDimension a dqv:Dimension ;
  skos:prefLabel "Epistemic weight"@en-GB ;
  skos:definition "How strongly the project believes a Finding / how reliable a Source is — the 0..1 confidence axis."@en-GB .

pkg:EpistemicBasisDimension a dqv:Dimension ;
  skos:prefLabel "Epistemic basis"@en-GB ;
  skos:definition "The KIND of grounds a Finding rests on — proven vs claimed vs conjectured (the categorical assurance axis, orthogonal to numeric weight)."@en-GB .

# The named metrics in those dimensions (instances of dqv:Metric). pkg:assurance is
# itself the categorical metric (typed dqv:Metric above); these two cover the numeric
# weight axis for the two subjects it attaches to.
pkg:ConfidenceMeasurement a dqv:Metric ;
  rdfs:label "Finding-confidence metric"@en-GB ;
  dqv:inDimension pkg:EpistemicWeightDimension ;
  rdfs:comment "The metric a Finding's pkg:confidence measures: the agent's epistemic weight on the Finding (0..1). A reified dqv:QualityMeasurement dqv:isMeasurementOf this metric, dqv:computedOn the Finding, dqv:value the confidence decimal."@en-GB .

pkg:SourceReliabilityMeasurement a dqv:Metric ;
  rdfs:label "Source-reliability metric"@en-GB ;
  dqv:inDimension pkg:EpistemicWeightDimension ;
  rdfs:comment "The metric a Source's pkg:confidence measures: how reliable the source is (0..1). Same DQV shape as pkg:ConfidenceMeasurement, distinct subject + dimension role."@en-GB .

pkg:discoveredFrom a owl:ObjectProperty ;
  rdfs:label "discovered from"@en-GB ;
  rdfs:comment "The source / activity a Finding (or Task) was discovered from. rdfs:subPropertyOf prov:wasDerivedFrom so the SHACL minCount-1 source guardrail is satisfied by either form."@en-GB ;
  rdfs:subPropertyOf prov:wasDerivedFrom .

# =============================================================================
# Algorithm / Technique — reuse CiTO (cito:extends / cito:usesMethodIn) +
# dcterms:replaces / skos:related / schema:SoftwareSourceCode; the ONLY bespoke term is
# couldBeMergedWith, reserved for genuine merge-candidacy (sq-2489d.3: lean on the
# established SPAR CiTO relations rather than minting bespoke method-relation predicates)
# =============================================================================

pkg:Technique a owl:Class ;
  rdfs:label "Technique"@en-GB ;
  rdfs:comment "An algorithm / technique / method the project knows about. The typed RELATIONS between Techniques reuse the established SPAR CiTO terms wherever they fit (sq-2489d.3), so no bespoke method-relation predicate is minted: extends = cito:extends (this technique extends ideas in another); uses-method-in = cito:usesMethodIn (employs a methodology documented in another); supersedes = dcterms:replaces (inverse dcterms:isReplacedBy); alternative-to = skos:related; implemented-by = pkg:implementedBy -> schema:SoftwareSourceCode. The bespoke pkg:couldBeMergedWith is RESERVED for the genuine, forward-looking merge-candidacy hint that CiTO has no symmetric term for."@en-GB ;
  rdfs:subClassOf skos:Concept .

pkg:implementedBy a owl:ObjectProperty ;
  rdfs:label "implemented by"@en-GB ;
  rdfs:comment "The code (a crate / module / PR) that implements a Technique. Range schema:SoftwareSourceCode; the implementing PR is recorded as a prov:Activity via prov:wasGeneratedBy."@en-GB ;
  rdfs:domain pkg:Technique ;
  rdfs:range schema:SoftwareSourceCode .

# --- NET-NEW: symmetric merge hint between two Techniques.
pkg:couldBeMergedWith a owl:ObjectProperty , owl:SymmetricProperty ;
  rdfs:label "could be merged with"@en-GB ;
  rdfs:comment "NET-NEW. A forward-looking, symmetric hint that two Techniques might be merged into one. No established precedent (skos:related is weaker / not symmetric-by-design for a merge-candidacy claim), so it is minted as an owl:SymmetricProperty. Per the design §2.5, prefer asserting it AS a pkg:Finding (carrying evidence + confidence) over a bare triple."@en-GB ;
  rdfs:domain pkg:Technique ;
  rdfs:range pkg:Technique .

# =============================================================================
# Task — the bd model -> RDF (schema.org status + DC structure); the SINGLE
# dependency inverse pair, fixed once (§2.2)
# =============================================================================

pkg:Task a owl:Class ;
  rdfs:label "Task"@en-GB ;
  rdfs:comment "A unit of project work — the RDF projection of a bd issue (tasks + dependsOn/blockedBy + status + type + priority + parent-child + discovered-from + related). rdfs:subClassOf schema:Action. The PKG MIRRORS bd as a read-model; bd remains the source-of-record (design §4)."@en-GB ;
  rdfs:subClassOf schema:Action .

# --- the single inverse pair (§2.2). pkg:dependsOn (a task waits on its
#     dependency) and its OWL inverse pkg:blockedBy. There is NO pkg:blocks:
#     bd's `blocks` edge is the inverse-of-dependsOn direction, modelled as
#     pkg:blockedBy. Every constraint / query names ONLY these two predicates.
pkg:dependsOn a owl:ObjectProperty ;
  rdfs:label "depends on"@en-GB ;
  rdfs:comment "NET-NEW. This task waits on its dependency (the dependency must close first). owl:inverseOf pkg:blockedBy. bd's `blocks` edge is modelled in this direction; there is deliberately NO pkg:blocks predicate."@en-GB ;
  owl:inverseOf pkg:blockedBy ;
  rdfs:domain pkg:Task ;
  rdfs:range pkg:Task .

pkg:blockedBy a owl:ObjectProperty ;
  rdfs:label "blocked by"@en-GB ;
  rdfs:comment "NET-NEW. The OWL inverse of pkg:dependsOn: this task is blocked by another. (?a pkg:blockedBy ?b) <=> (?b pkg:dependsOn ?a)."@en-GB ;
  rdfs:domain pkg:Task ;
  rdfs:range pkg:Task .

pkg:status a owl:ObjectProperty ;
  rdfs:label "status"@en-GB ;
  rdfs:comment "The task status (pkg:Open | pkg:InProgress | pkg:Blocked | pkg:Deferred | pkg:Closed). A SKOS-scheme concept; aligned to schema.org ActionStatusType."@en-GB ;
  rdfs:domain pkg:Task ;
  rdfs:range skos:Concept .

pkg:issueType a owl:ObjectProperty ;
  rdfs:label "issue type"@en-GB ;
  rdfs:comment "The bd issue_type (pkg:Bug | pkg:Feature | pkg:Task | pkg:Epic | pkg:Chore | pkg:Decision | pkg:Milestone | pkg:Spike)."@en-GB ;
  rdfs:domain pkg:Task ;
  rdfs:range skos:Concept .

pkg:priority a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
  rdfs:label "priority"@en-GB ;
  rdfs:comment "The bd priority (integer; lower = higher priority). The SHACL TaskShape bounds it to 0..4."@en-GB ;
  rdfs:domain pkg:Task ;
  rdfs:range xsd:integer .

pkg:surface a owl:ObjectProperty ;
  rdfs:label "surface"@en-GB ;
  rdfs:comment "The project surface a Task touches (mirrors a bd area:* label). A skos:Concept in pkg:Surfaces."@en-GB ;
  rdfs:domain pkg:Task ;
  rdfs:range skos:Concept .

pkg:label a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
  rdfs:label "label"@en-GB ;
  rdfs:comment "A free-form bd label string (e.g. \"needs:human-review\"). The §4.1 frontier query filters human-gated tasks via STRSTARTS over these."@en-GB ;
  rdfs:domain pkg:Task ;
  rdfs:range xsd:string .

# --- status scheme (skos; aligned to schema.org ActionStatusType) ---
pkg:Statuses a skos:ConceptScheme ; rdfs:label "Task status scheme"@en-GB .
pkg:Open a skos:Concept ; skos:inScheme pkg:Statuses ; skos:prefLabel "Open"@en-GB ;
  skos:closeMatch schema:PotentialActionStatus .
pkg:InProgress a skos:Concept ; skos:inScheme pkg:Statuses ; skos:prefLabel "In progress"@en-GB ;
  skos:closeMatch schema:ActiveActionStatus .
pkg:Blocked a skos:Concept ; skos:inScheme pkg:Statuses ; skos:prefLabel "Blocked"@en-GB .
pkg:Deferred a skos:Concept ; skos:inScheme pkg:Statuses ; skos:prefLabel "Deferred"@en-GB .
pkg:Closed a skos:Concept ; skos:inScheme pkg:Statuses ; skos:prefLabel "Closed"@en-GB ;
  skos:closeMatch schema:CompletedActionStatus .

# --- issue-type scheme (skos) ---
pkg:IssueTypes a skos:ConceptScheme ; rdfs:label "Issue type scheme"@en-GB .
pkg:Bug a skos:Concept ; skos:inScheme pkg:IssueTypes ; skos:prefLabel "Bug"@en-GB .
pkg:Feature a skos:Concept ; skos:inScheme pkg:IssueTypes ; skos:prefLabel "Feature"@en-GB .
pkg:Chore a skos:Concept ; skos:inScheme pkg:IssueTypes ; skos:prefLabel "Chore"@en-GB .
pkg:Decision a skos:Concept ; skos:inScheme pkg:IssueTypes ; skos:prefLabel "Decision"@en-GB .
pkg:Milestone a skos:Concept ; skos:inScheme pkg:IssueTypes ; skos:prefLabel "Milestone"@en-GB .
pkg:Spike a skos:Concept ; skos:inScheme pkg:IssueTypes ; skos:prefLabel "Spike"@en-GB .
pkg:Epic a skos:Concept ; skos:inScheme pkg:IssueTypes ; skos:prefLabel "Epic"@en-GB .
# NOTE: pkg:Task (the issue-type individual "task") would collide with the pkg:Task
# CLASS, so the bd "task" issue_type is modelled as the class itself being the default;
# a Task with no pkg:issueType is an ordinary task. The named individuals above cover
# the non-default bd types.

# --- surface scheme (skos; mirrors bd area:* labels) ---
pkg:Surfaces a skos:ConceptScheme ; rdfs:label "Project surface scheme"@en-GB .
